{"id":"src/components/ImageGuard.tsx","pkg":"src/components","kind":"ui","lines":23,"commentLines":5,"header":["THE BROWSER SIDE OF \"PHOTOGRAPHS CANNOT BE SAVED\" (rules and limits: src/lib/ui/imageGuard.ts; the CSS side, no dragging and nothing printed, is in globals.css). It is mounted once in the root layout. Anywhere in the app it refuses, the right-click menu and the drag of a picture (an <img>, a <canvas>, a <video>, or anything inside a picture's frame). I listen in the capture phase on the document, so a picture added later is covered too, and I never touch the page's own clicks (a picture still opens full size when it is clicked)."],"symbols":[{"name":"ImageGuard","kind":"component","exported":true,"isDefault":true,"async":false,"line":11,"sig":"export default function ImageGuard()","params":[],"returns":"","generics":"","doc":[],"paramDocs":{},"returnDoc":"","id":"de2cd3f997-ImageGuard","usedBy":["src/app/layout.tsx"]}],"imports":[{"file":"src/lib/ui/imageGuard.ts","names":["isGuardedElement"],"lazy":false}],"importedBy":["src/app/layout.tsx"],"external":["react"],"reexports":[],"tests":[],"behaviours":[]}